Linh (SRE): FYI scheduled maintenance + planned failover + load test for Dedicated GPU pool A on Tue Mar 24 02:00-02:45 UTC. Expect short (30-90s) controlled failovers per AZ, plus a phased traffic soak. :rotating_light;
Linh (SRE): Impact: potential 50-150ms added tail latency for a subset of requests, maybe a handful of transient 5xx while we drain and reprovision. No customer-facing downtime expected, but we'll monitor.;
Raj (on-call): What's the exact rollout plan? Are we doing canary first or all AZs at once?;
Linh (SRE): Canary in us-west-2 first (10% capacity), then us-east-1, then eu-west-1. Each canary window ~10m with smoke checks. If checks fail we abort and rollback.;
Ana (Platform): Will routing do automatic fallback to compatible model variants? Need to confirm path for private deployments.;
Linh (SRE): Yes — smart routing will route to compatible variants. Private deployments with VPC control plane: ops will be notified, but they need to opt-in for failover. We're sending customer notice to whitelist list.;
Michael (ENG): I'll own the smoke test harness. What's the smoke checklist?;
Linh (SRE): Smoke checklist (short):
- check 200s for /v1/generate on canary
- verify KV cache warm within 2x baseline
- 5m of error-rate < 0.5% per route
- latency p95 within +150ms of baseline
- ingest internal health-check events to datadog;
Linh (SRE): I'll post the runbook link in a sec. Oncall will have escalation: if error rate spikes >1% for 5m, escalate to SRE lead and stop rollout.;
oncall-bot: Scheduled maintenance event created: id=mt-20260324-01, calendar invite + public status page update queued.;
Raj (on-call): Noted. I'll be on shift for the window. Can we also throttle non-critical background jobs during this to avoid noise?;
Ana (Platform): Yes, we'll pause nightly retrain and large batch embedding jobs 30m before and after. I'll update the job-scheduler.;
Michael (ENG): Also we'll run a short synthetic load test (20m) after canary to validate autoscaler behavior. Will use smaller request sizes to avoid costs.;
Linh (SRE): Good. Post-checks: final signoff by SRE lead, then proceed to full rollout. If anything funky, revert to previous instance group within 2m using snapshot restore.;
Raj (on-call): SLA question: Do we need to notify any customers with reserved Dedicated contracts?;
Linh (SRE): Yes — support is sending an email to impacted Dedicated tenants now. Ops has an FAQ snippet if customers call.;
oncall-bot: Reminder: add postmortem template link to thread after window.;
Ana (Platform): Logging note: make sure we capture KV cache hits/misses and kernel select metrics during the soak. I added those to the dashboard.;
Michael (ENG): I'll be in the war room channel for the window: #release-war-room.;
Linh (SRE): Thanks everyone. Running final preflight at 01:15 UTC. I'll post 'GO' here 30m before. :thumbsup:
